    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2771A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act authorizing a certain housing authority to sell or lease all or\npart of a certain housing project\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nAuthorizes the Albany Housing Authority to sell or lease all or a part\nof the project known as the Ezra Prentice Homes for the purpose of\nrehabilitation of the project.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 sets out the legislative findings. Section 2 authorizes the\nAlbany Housing Authority, with the approval of the commissioner of\nhousing and community renewal, to sell or lease all or part of the\nEzra Prentice Homes in the city of Albany for the purpose of\nrehabilitating the project for low income families. Section 3\nestablishes the guidelines for occupancy to ensure that the units\nremain affordable and that all laws rules and regulations applicable\nto federal public housing projects continue to apply after the sale or\nlease of the project. Section 4 continues state subsidies for debt\nservice on outstanding bonds, notes or other obligations. Section 5 is\nthe effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nEzra Prentice Homes was built in the early 1970's on South Pearl\nStreet in Albany, and provides 179 units of affordable housing for\nfamilies. These units are in dire need of rehabilitation.  Albany's\npublic housing occupancy rate is 99%, with the longest waiting lists\nthe Albany Housing Authority has ever seen.\n\nThe Authority has been developing this project for several years and\nhas finally been able to secure approximately $12 million to move\nforward with the project.  However, the final piece to make this\nproject viable is to allow the division of housing and community\nrenewal to consent to transfer this project to a privately owned\nentity in order to raise the rehabilitation capital through the sale\nof 4% low income housing tax credits.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the state\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately, provided, however, that the provisions of section 4 of\nthis act shall apply to any debt service payments which become due\nafter such date.\n",
